# Echo campaign A, "old setup": the connect test of the MIPRO 2024 echo paper (github.com/joegharbi/echo_server),
# now with BEAM busy-waiting on and off. TCP echo servers in C, Java and Erlang (benchmarks/echo/); every server as
# built and Erlang also as -nobw (C and Java have no such setting and are skipped), each in Docker and natively,
# in one shuffled order. Every client connects, sends "Hello, Servers!" (15 B), waits for its echo, disconnects.
# 4 tests x 4 servers x 2 deployments x 5 repeats = 160 measurements, about 15 h (10,000 clients spaced alone ~11 h).
#   make run CONFIG=campaigns/paper/echo-old.config
# Decisions (2026-10-16, after the supervisor meeting):
#   - client counts: the ones all three servers share in the old paper's results (sleep 100, 1000, 10000) and the
#     paper's nosleep count (4000)
#   - nosleep is one round, as in the old paper: all clients finish within ~2 s, so few meter samples (campaign B
#     repeats the round to fix that)
#   - same machine settings as the busy-wait campaign: CPU fixed at 1800 MHz, 5 repeats, no idle measurement
MACHINE=minimal
ENV_CPU_SPEED=1800
MEASURE=echo
VARIANTS=nobw:ERL_FLAGS=+sbwt none +sbwtdcpu none +sbwtdio none
DEPLOY=container native
REPEATS=5
IDLE_SECONDS=0
# "sleep": clients start 0.1 s apart (100 clients = 10 s of load, 1000 = 100 s, 10000 = 1000 s)
ECHO_CONNECT_CLIENTS=100 1000 10000
ECHO_CONNECT_SPACING_SECONDS=0.1
# "nosleep": all 4000 clients at once
ECHO_NOSLEEP_CLIENTS=4000
ECHO_NOSLEEP_ROUNDS=1
# The old paper had only the connect test
ECHO_BURST_CLIENTS=
ECHO_STREAM_CLIENTS=
ECHO_SIZES_BYTES=15
